Text:
fearlessManager is a program. When it starts it attempts to become the 'single' manager.
The 'single' manager applies the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
The 'manager path' is the OS path of the ManagerFolder on the actual file system.
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library.
We expect that only the manager can edit this file.
The Info of projects.info is a ProjectsInfo.
fearlessManager.names is a map from ProjectName to TaggedText, held in memory only.
fearlessManager.states is a map from TaggedText to State, held in memory only.
fearlessManager$Message calls the method corresponding to that message.
fearlessManager$show if Message is Show,
fearlessManager$show(ProjectName) if Message is Show ProjectName; etc.
fearlessManager$accept(Message) runs right before the first Output of fearlessManager$Message, or when fearlessManager$Message ends with no Output and no fearlessManager$refuse(Message, RefusedError).
fearlessManager ends Message.connection when fearlessManager$receive(Message) ends.

Grammar:
ManagerFolder ::= LockFile, "projects.info", "icons", "locks"
//icons and locks are folders.
LockFile ::= "no_manager.lock" | "candidate_manager.lock" | "single_manager_at_", Port, ".lock"
//the syntax of LockFile defines a file name.
Port ::= [1-9][0-9]*//the digits are a port of the loopback address
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.map("projects", Projects, "reserve", Extensions)
Projects ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn) //using .list/.map loosely: assuming any arity is allowed
Extensions ::= Infos.list(Extension1 .. Extensionn) //1..n can be empty, Infos.list() == Info
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)
Project ::= Infos.map("path", TaggedText, "kind", Kind, "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, ProjectName1 .. TypeNamen, ProjectNamen)
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
Extension ::= OSExtension
ProjectName ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]*
TaggedText ::= \
  Base16                                 \
  | "Str:", EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn \
  | "UStr:", EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn
EscapedChar ::= [0-9A-Za-z +\-*/=<>,.;:()\[\]{}`'"!?@#$%^&_|~\\]
ProgressLine ::= implementation dependent progress information cap to 80 chars.
State ::= "unreachable" | "invalid ", Error | "outOfDate" | "compiled" | "idle" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
NameError ::= ...

Well formedness:
in Port: the digits form a number smaller than 65536.
in Extension: not in "fearless" or "ffile000"-"ffile999" or "fapp000"-"fapp999".
in Projects: no two Project with equal TaggedText.
in Extensions: all Extension are disjoint.
in Project: all TypeName in TypeNames are disjoint.
in ProjectName: ProjectName, ".fearless" is a ValidSegment.
in TaggedText: starts with "Str:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path.
in TaggedText: starts with "UStr:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path, and p.isStr is False.
in TaggedText: is a Base16 only if no Fearless UStr encodes the path it decodes to.

Text:
Examples of the TaggedText of a path:
C:\data\hello -> Str:"C:\data\hello"
/x/a"b -> Str:`/x/a"b`
/tmp/a, a new line, b -> Str:"/tmp/a" | "b"
/tmp/a, a new line -> Str:"/tmp/a"|
/x/caf, U+00E9 -> UStr:"/x/caf".u"00E9"
/x/a, U+F066, b -> UStr:"/x/a".u"F066"+("b".u)
/x/, the byte FF, on Linux -> Base16:2F782FFF
In the text of projects.info, Str:"C:\data\hello" is "Str:\"C:\\data\\hello\"".

Invariant:
At every moment, at most one fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C action fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder with files: \
  empty no_manager.lock,\
  projects.info holding Infos.map("projects", Infos.list(), "reserve", Infos.list()),\
  and the empty folders icons and locks.
D action fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
E action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C event Another process creates a folder at the 'manager path' before fearlessManager\
  creates the ManagerFolder.
D action fearlessManager ends.

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile called no_manager.lock,\
  and no process holds the lock of no_manager.lock.
C action fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
D action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile called candidate_manager.lock\
  or single_manager_at_X.lock, and no process holds the lock of that LockFile.
C action fearlessManager takes the lock of that LockFile.
D action fearlessManager renames that LockFile to no_manager.lock.
E action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A fact Another process holds the lock of the LockFile of the folder at the 'manager path'.
B action fearlessManager ends.

Story:
A fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds no LockFile, or more than one LockFile.
B action fearlessManager$fatalError('manager path', "the folder is not a ManagerFolder")

Define fearlessManager$serve():
A fact fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the\
  'manager path' is a ManagerFolder.
B action fearlessManager renames no_manager.lock to candidate_manager.lock.
C action fearlessManager copies base.IconsConflict and base.IconsFearless into icons.
D action For each Project of projects.info with the Kind code: Coordinator$dropUnfinished(Project."path").
E action fearlessManager$readNames()
F action fearlessManager$buildMap()
G action fearlessManager listens for connections on the loopback address,\
  on a port X that the OS picks.
H action fearlessManager renames candidate_manager.lock to single_manager_at_X.lock.
I after fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.
J action fearlessManager shows its tray icon.
K action For each Message arriving on port X, one at a time, in the order the messages arrive: fearlessManager$receive(Message).

Define fearlessManager$serve():
A fact fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the\
  'manager path' is not a ManagerFolder.
B action fearlessManager$fatalError('manager path', "the folder is not a ManagerFolder")

Define fearlessManager$save(ProjectsInfo):
A action fearlessManager replaces projects.info with ProjectsInfo.
B action fearlessManager$readNames()
C action For each Project of projects.info: fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project)

Define fearlessManager$readNames():
A action fearlessManager.names= {}
B action For each Project of projects.info where the folder at Project."path" holds ProjectName.fearless and no other *.fearless,\
  and the folder of no other Project holds ProjectName.fearless: fearlessManager.names+= (ProjectName->Project."path")

Notation: projectNames(Message) = the ProjectNames of Message where:
- Message runs no main.
Notation: projectNames(Message) = the ProjectNames of Message, then the ProjectNames of Project."mounts" where:
- Message runs a main of Project.

Define fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName):
A fact (ProjectName->Project."path") in fearlessManager.names.
B fact The folder at Project."path" holds ProjectName.fearless and no other *.fearless.
C action return Project

Define fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName):
A fact (ProjectName->Project."path") in fearlessManager.names.
B fact The folder at Project."path" does not hold ProjectName.fearless, or holds another *.fearless.
C action fearlessManager$readNames()
D action return fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName)

Define fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName):
A fact (ProjectName->_) not in fearlessManager.names.
B action fearlessManager$readNames()
C fact (ProjectName->_) in fearlessManager.names.
D action return fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName)

Notation: fearlessManager.projectOf(Base16) = Project where:
- Base16 and Project."path" encode the same path, for a Project of projects.info.

Define fearlessManager$receive(Message):
A fact fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName) is undefined, for a ProjectName of projectNames(Message).
B action fearlessManager$refuse(Message, "no registered project is named "+ProjectName)

Define fearlessManager$receive(Message):
A fact Message is Forget Base16 or Fix Base16, and fearlessManager.projectOf(Base16) is undefined.
B action fearlessManager$refuse(Message, "no registered project is at "+the path of Base16)

Define fearlessManager$receive(Message):
A fact No other Define of fearlessManager$receive(Message) holds.
B action For each ProjectName of projectNames(Message): fearlessManager$autoCheck(fearlessManager$projectOf(ProjectName))
C action fearlessManager$Message -> Message.connection

Define fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project):
A fact The folder at Project."path" can not be reached.
B action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->"unreachable")
C action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)

Define fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project):
A fact The folder at Project."path" can be reached.
B fact A Compile of Project runs, or a main with a dataEdit mount of Project runs.

Define fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project):
A fact The folder at Project."path" can be reached.
B fact No Compile of Project runs, and no main with a dataEdit mount of Project runs.
C action fearlessManager$checkName(Project)

Define fearlessManager$checkName(Project):
A fact (ProjectName->Project."path") in fearlessManager.names.
B fact The folder at Project."path" holds ProjectName.fearless and no other *.fearless.
C action fearlessManager$checkContent(Project)

Define fearlessManager$checkName(Project):
A fact (ProjectName->Project."path") in fearlessManager.names.
B fact The folder at Project."path" does not hold ProjectName.fearless, or holds another *.fearless.
C action fearlessManager$readNames()
D action fearlessManager$checkName(Project)

Define fearlessManager$checkName(Project):
A fact (_->Project."path") not in fearlessManager.names.
B action fearlessManager$readNames()
C fact (_->Project."path") in fearlessManager.names.
D action fearlessManager$checkName(Project)

Define fearlessManager$checkName(Project):
A fact (_->Project."path") not in fearlessManager.names.
B action fearlessManager$readNames()
C fact (_->Project."path") not in fearlessManager.names.
D action fearlessManager$invalid(Project, Error), for Error listing the *.fearless in Project."path" and the other folders holding them.

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is code, and Coordinator$check(Project."path") gives Invalid(Error).
B action fearlessManager$invalid(Project, Error)

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is code, and Coordinator$check(Project."path") gives OutOfDate.
B action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->"outOfDate")
C action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is code, and Coordinator$check(Project."path") gives Compiled.
B action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->"compiled")

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is dataRead or dataEdit, and FolderShapes$check(Project."path") gives Error.
B action fearlessManager$invalid(Project, Error)

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is dataRead or dataEdit, and FolderShapes$check(Project."path") gives no Error.
B action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->Project."kind")

Define fearlessManager$checkContent(Project):
A fact Project."kind" is idle.
B action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->"idle")

Define fearlessManager$invalid(Project, Error):
A action fearlessManager.states+= (Project."path"->"invalid "+Error)
B action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)
C action Coordinator$writeError(Project."path", Error)

Story:
A event A Compile of Project ends.
B action fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project)

Story:
A fact managerGUI? is not empty.
B action Every 3 seconds: fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project), for the next Project of projects.info, in turn.

Define fearlessManager$accept(Message):
A action fearlessManager sends "Applied" -> Message.connection
B action fearlessManager sends "Applied"+Message."what part of it?" -> managerGUI?.connection
//above managerGUI?.connection is an 'trash all' connection if managerGUI? == empty

Define fearlessManager$refuse(Message, RefusedError):
A action fearlessManager sends "Refused"+RefusedError -> Message.connection
B action fearlessManager sends "Refused"+RefusedError+Message."what part of it?" -> managerGUI?.connection

Define fearlessManager$show():
A action managerGUI? = ManagerGui$startIfEmpty(managerGUI?) //else identity

Define fearlessManager$quit():
A action fearlessManager renames single_manager_at_X.lock to no_manager.lock
B action fearlessManager stops listening to X.
C action For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager$terminate(p).//async calls
D action fearlessManager sends an up to date ProgressLine -> Quit.connection\
  every 2 seconds, until fearlessManager ends.
E after all projects are fully terminated
F action fearlessManager ends.

Define fearlessManager$forget(Base16):
A fact fearlessManager.projectOf(Base16) gives Project.
B action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)
C action fearlessManager$save(the Info of projects.info without Project)

Define fearlessManager$fix(Base16):
A fact fearlessManager.projectOf(Base16) gives Project.
B action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)
C action fearlessManager.names-= (_->Project."path")
D action FolderShapes$fix(Project."path")
E fact fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(Project."path") gives ProjectName.
F action fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project)

Define fearlessManager$fix(Base16):
A fact fearlessManager.projectOf(Base16) gives Project.
B action fearlessManager$terminate(Project)
C action fearlessManager.names-= (_->Project."path")
D action FolderShapes$fix(Project."path")
E fact fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(Project."path") gives NameError.
F action fearlessManager writes NameError in the Output of Project.
G action fearlessManager$autoCheck(Project)

Define fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(TaggedText):
A fact The folder at TaggedText holds ProjectName.fearless and no other *.fearless.
B fact (ProjectName->_) not in fearlessManager.names.
C action fearlessManager.names+= (ProjectName->TaggedText)
D action return ProjectName

Define fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(TaggedText):
A fact The folder at TaggedText holds no *.fearless.
B fact ProjectName is the last segment of the path of TaggedText.
C fact (ProjectName->_) not in fearlessManager.names.
D action fearlessManager writes the file ProjectName.fearless in the folder at TaggedText;\
  the file ProjectName.fearless will contain exactly a new line.
E action fearlessManager.names+= (ProjectName->TaggedText)
F action return ProjectName

Define fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(TaggedText):
A fact The folder at TaggedText holds no *.fearless.
B fact ProjectName is the last segment of the path of TaggedText.
C fact (ProjectName->_) in fearlessManager.names.
D action fearlessManager writes the file ProjectName2.fearless in the folder at TaggedText;\
  the file ProjectName2.fearless will contain exactly a new line.
E action fearlessManager.names+= (ProjectName2->TaggedText)
F action return ProjectName2

Define fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(TaggedText):
A fact No other Define of fearlessManager$forgeProjectName(TaggedText) holds.
B action return NameError

Define fearlessManager$fatalError(FatalError):
A action fearlessManager shows FatalError.dialog(busyProjects.names).
B action The user closes the dialog.
C action fearlessManager$reset()

Define fearlessManager$reset():
A action fearlessManager renames single_manager_at_X.lock to no_manager.lock
C action fearlessManager stops listening to X.
D action For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager$terminate(p).//async calls
E after all projects are fully terminated
F action Reconciliator$eradicateAll
G action fearlessManager deletes the folder at the 'manager path'.
H action fearlessManager ends.

Implementation notes:
The 'manager path' is the folder fearless<version> next to the program folder, the folder holding fearlessManager, fearlessMessage and fearlessOnClick.
fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder by filling a new folder next to the 'manager path', then renaming that new folder to the 'manager path': the rename fails when a folder is at the 'manager path' already.
The lock of a LockFile is the lock of FileChannel.tryLock: the OS releases the lock when the process ends, however the process ends, and the lock follows the file when the file is renamed.
